        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(hooks): wire message:sending internal hook to user-defined hooks",
        "body": "## Problem\n\nThe `message:sending` internal hook was not wired to user-defined hooks, so custom hooks that subscribed to outgoing message events never fired. This prevented users from implementing message logging, content filtering, or outbound audit hooks.\n\n## Root Cause\n\n`internal-hooks.ts` defined the `message:sending` hook type but `deliver.ts` never invoked it when sending outbound messages — the hook was registered but the call site was missing.\n\n## Fix\n\nWire the `message:sending` internal hook to the outbound message delivery path in `deliver.ts`, so user-defined hooks receive outgoing message events.\n\n## Real Behavior Proof\n\n### Test Results (vitest 4.1.8)\n\n```\n$ vitest run --config test/vitest/vitest.hooks.config.ts \\\n    src/hooks/internal-hooks.test.ts\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  36 passed (36)\n\n$ vitest run --config test/vitest/vitest.infra.config.ts \\\n    src/infra/outbound/deliver.test.ts\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  96 passed (96)\n```\n\n**Total: 132 tests passed across 2 test files.**\n\n### Before/After\n\n**Before:** `message:sending` hook defined but never called during outbound delivery. User hooks subscribed to this event silently never fired.\n\n**After:** `message:sending` hook fires for every outbound message, allowing user-defined hooks to intercept, log, filter, or audit outgoing messages.\n\nFixes #29365",
        "branch": "fix/message-sending-hook",
